From 8b71b50fa6552c2f3b9e75a1473a4466283c1cba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean Carey <seankojicarey@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:04:16 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Never clean up a worktree recreated at the recorded path

A run-owned worktree was identified by its admin directory path and the
inode numbers of that directory and its .git file. ext4 hands freed inode
numbers to the next new file, so a worktree removed and recreated at the
same path matched the recorded identity and cleanup offered
`git worktree remove` for it.

Recording a worktree now writes a random token into its private admin
directory and keeps it in the identity. `git worktree remove` and
`git worktree prune` delete that directory, so a recreated worktree has no
token and is reported as replaced. Identities recorded before this change
are compared on the fields they have.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
